      "name": "ProcessTileComponent",
      "signature": "void ProcessTileComponent(void * pTileComp)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompresses and loads tile component mipmap data from compressed format.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. If cache index (param +0x4) is negative, error assert and exit\n  2. If cache index is 0, decompress tile data: read pair of (skip_count, copy_count)\n     bytes from source (param +0x10), write decompressed bytes to buffer DAT_6f884e08\n  3. Allocate new cache slot by calling FUN_6f876c90\n  4. Validate allocated index is within range (0 to DAT_6f885354-1)\n  5. Store param reference in cache at offset *(DAT_6f88536c + cache_index*0x14 - 0xc)\n  6. Download mipmap level 3 using grTexDownloadMipMap\n  7. Set texture source with grTexSource\n  8. Call FUN_6f8729e0 for finalization\n\n  Parameters:\n    pTileComp  cache index and source data pointer\n               +0x4: short cache index (0 = needs decompression, <0 = error)\n               +0x10: byte* pointer to compressed source data\n\n  Returns:\n    void (modifies global texture state via grTexDownloadMipMap, grTexSource)\n\n  Special Cases:\n    Negative cache index triggers assert and FUN_6f878859(-1)\n    Decompression uses run-length encoding: 2-byte header per row\n    Each row can have multiple skip/copy pairs\n    32 rows of 0x20 (32) bytes each",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3b428f516ffab3c9346f95d2ab3569e9",
