      "name": "RemoveInventoryItems",
      "signature": "void RemoveInventoryItems(int * pInventory)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes all items from an inventory structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if inventory has a primary item (offset 0x42)\n  2. If yes, call removal function for that item (decrement by 1)\n  3. Iterate through inventory item array (offset 0x54)\n  4. For each item with count > 0, call removal function\n  5. Increment loop counter and array pointer (+0x14 per entry)\n\nParameters:\n  pInventory (ECX): Pointer to inventory structure\n    Offset 0x42: short - primary item count\n    Offset 0x50: int   - number of items in array\n    Offset 0x54: int*  - pointer to item array\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field           |Type      |Description\n  0x42  |2   |wItemCount      |short     |Primary item count\n  0x50  |4   |nItemArraySize  |int       |Number of items\n  0x54  |4   |pItemArray      |void*     |Pointer to item array\n  \nItem Array Entry Layout (stride 0x14 bytes):\n  Offset|Field              |Type       |Description\n  0x00  |nUnknown           |dword      |Unknown field\n  0x04  |wItemCountPerSlot  |short      |Item count in this slot\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - If primary item count is 0, skips primary item removal\n  - If item array size is 0, loop is skipped\n  - Items with count <= 0 are skipped during iteration\n  - Calls 0x6f874320 and 0x6f876e70 for linked list removal",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:924084ab11c7212b7fbff95b16b8c898",
