      "name": "InitializeGlideWindowInternal",
      "signature": "int InitializeGlideWindowInternal(dword dwBinkRender, int nScreenMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize Glide graphics window for rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if window already open; log error and return if so\n  2. Call internal setup routine (FUN_6f872da0)\n  3. Set screen dimensions based on mode (640x480 or 800x600)\n  4. Set fullscreen flag based on mode (0/2 = fullscreen, others = windowed)\n  5. Open Glide window via grSstWinOpen()\n  6. If opened successfully, query and log GPU capabilities\n  7. Configure vertex layout, coordinate space, color/depth masks\n  8. Set texture filters and chromakey value\n  9. Calculate texture memory alignment and allocate TMU memory blocks\n  10. Initialize texture memory pools based on screen mode\n  11. Call finalization routine (FUN_6f874f60) and set game mode\n  12. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwBinkRender  [ECX]: Bink renderer flag (passed to grSstWinOpen)\n  nScreenMode   [EDX]: Screen mode: 0=640x480 fullscreen, 2=640x480 fullscreen,\n                       other=800x600 windowed\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1: Window initialized successfully\n  EAX=0: Window already open or grSstWinOpen failed or insufficient GPU memory\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_bGlideWindowOpen already set, logs assertion and returns 0\n  - If GPU insufficient memory for textures, logs warning and returns 0\n  - Queries TMU count (0-3) and clamps to 3 maximum\n  - Sets DAT_6f8814b0 to prevent repeated GPU capability queries",
