      "name": "CloseGlideWindow",
      "signature": "dword CloseGlideWindow(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Closes the Glide rendering window and cleans up associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if Glide window is open; return 1 (success) if not\n  2. Mark window as closed and log closure message\n  3. Call grFinish() to flush pending rendering commands\n  4. Destroy graphics resources based on hardware/software configuration:\n     - If hardware mode (g_bUseHardware=0): Call FUN_6f874800()\n     - Otherwise: Destroy texture and chroma key resources with FUN_6f873ff0/6f876c00\n  5. Destroy lighting resources (light maps, ambient/direct lights) with FUN_6f877130()\n  6. Prepare for final cleanup with FUN_6f875020()\n  7. Retry closing the Glide state up to 100 (0x64) times:\n     - Call grSstWinClose() to close the state\n     - Exit loop if successful (return value = 1)\n     - Continue retrying if still open\n  8. If max retries exceeded: Log failure message\n  9. Final cleanup: Call FUN_6f872f30(), clear render flag, log success message\n  10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 (success/window closed)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
