      "comment": "Handles pausing or resuming the Glide graphics window with thread safety.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Acquire critical section lock (g_pCriticalSection); assert if NULL\n  2. If bAbortGame is non-zero (abort mode):\n     - Close the Glide window via CloseGlideWindow()\n     - Set g_dwGameAbort = 1 (signal game abort)\n     - Release lock and return\n  3. If resume mode (bAbortGame = 0):\n     - If Glide window not already open, initialize via InitializeGlideWindowInternal()\n     - On successful init: clear buffers (grBufferClear) and swap (grBufferSwap)\n     - Set g_dwGameAbort = 0 (clear abort flag)\n  4. Release critical section lock\n\nParameters:\n  nBinkRender   [ECX] - Bink renderer flag passed to window initialization\n  nScreenMode   [EDX] - Screen mode: 0=640x480 fullscreen, 2=640x480 fullscreen,\n                        other=800x600 windowed\n  nAbortGame    [Stack] - Non-zero to abort/close, zero to resume/initialize\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pCriticalSection is NULL, triggers assertion with \"pcsPause\" message\n    at line 0x2C3 (707) in D2Gfx source, then recovers via FUN_6f878859(-1)\n  - Buffer swap uses g_pGraphicsConfig+0x10 to determine vsync flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:0b61e2de586e18b43b1d28bf3a98e0e2",
