      "name": "InitializeCharacterBitmap",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharacterBitmap(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds a character bitmap by rasterizing ASCII characters (0x20-0x7F) to buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Create device context for DISPLAY\n  2. Create Courier 10pt font (height 0xa, weight 0x190)\n  3. Create 8x16 monochrome bitmap (0x80 bytes per char)\n  4. Select font and bitmap into device context\n  5. Set text/background colors from global colors\n  6. Set background mode to TRANSPARENT (2)\n  7. Clear any existing character map (0x3000 bytes)\n  8. Allocate g_sgpCharMap = 0x3000 bytes\n  9. For each ASCII char (0x20-0x7F, count 0x60=96):\n     a. Draw character to bitmap\n     b. Scan 8x16 pixels: set buffer[offset] = 0xff if pixel matches\n        text color, else 0x0 (creates bitmap glyph)\n     c. Advance buffer offset by 0x80 bytes per character\n  10. Query character widths 0x20-0x7F to g_aCharWidths\n  11. Clean up: delete bitmap, font, device context\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Each glyph occupies 0x80 (128) bytes: 8 pixels wide * 16 pixels high\n  Total buffer size 0x3000 (12288) bytes = 96 chars * 128 bytes\n  If g_sgpCharMap already allocated, frees old buffer before realloc",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:9ea33b5eb9122db41177f3587e9c6aa1",
