      "name": "DrawRect",
      "signature": "void DrawRect(int nX1, float fHeight, int nY1, int nY2, dword dwColor, byte bAlpha)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws a filled rectangle or single point with specified color and alpha.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Validate coordinate bounds (0 to max in each dimension)\n    2. Get color value from parameter (param_1)\n    3. If alpha 0xFF, use alpha blend mode 0x1; else use 0x4\n    4. If both X coordinates equal and both Y coordinates equal, draw point\n    5. If X coordinates equal, draw vertical line\n    6. Else draw horizontal line or rectangle using grDrawPoint/grDrawLine\n\n  Parameters:\n    nX1 (ECX):   Starting X coordinate, must be >= 0 and < max_x\n    fHeight (EDX): Y coordinate or height value (float)\n    nY1 (Stack+4): Starting Y coordinate, must be >= 0 and < max_y\n    nY2 (Stack+8): Ending Y coordinate\n    dwColor (Stack+0xC): ARGB color value\n    bAlpha (Stack+0x10): Alpha value (0x00-0xFF); 0xFF = full alpha\n\n  Returns:\n    void (all paths return via RET 0x10)\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Both X equal AND both Y equal: draws single point at (X,Y)\n    - Both X equal: draws vertical line\n    - Both Y equal: draws horizontal line\n    - Otherwise: draws filled rectangle\n    - Alpha 0xFF uses SetAlphaBlendMode(0x1); other values use mode 0x4\n    - Invalid coordinates: returns without drawing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:18ca6a32f4e32e164a63ce46ff2ef4ab",
