      "name": "ReleasePoolItems",
      "signature": "void ReleasePoolItems(MemoryPool * pPool, BOOL fClear)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Release items from a memory pool and optionally clear the pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if fClear flag is non-zero; if zero, skip clearing and go to finalization\n  2. Loop through pool's free list (dwFreeCount times):\n     - Get next free item from pFirstFree (offset 0xc)\n     - Unlink item from current position in list\n     - Update doubly-linked list pointers (next at 0xc, prev at 0x10)\n     - Mark word at offset 0x42 as 0 (item cleared flag)\n  3. Move processed items to used list for rebalancing\n  4. Finalize: Check if pool data pointer (offset 0x1c) is set\n  5. If set, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free pool memory\n  6. Zero out entire pool structure header (8 DWORDs, 32 bytes total)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: pPool - Pointer to MemoryPool structure containing item lists\n  EDX: fClear - BOOL flag; non-zero to clear items, zero to finalize only\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; modifies pool structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - FogAssert called if free item count mismatches at 0xd3, 0x9f\n  - FUN_6f878859 called with -1 to get items when needed\n  - ReleasePoolAllocation called to free backing pool memory",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:f322827b5c360f78f005a4100cd3e4b7",
