      "comment": "Removes an item from a doubly-linked list by index\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if list count [ECX+0x8] is non-zero\n  2. Verify head pointer [ECX+0xc] is non-null\n  3. Calculate target node address: head + (nIndex * 0x14) bytes\n  4. If target is current head [ECX+0xc]:\n     - Update head to target->next [ESI+0xc]\n     - Clear prev/next pointers if next is null\n     - Clear prev pointer of next node if exists\n  5. Else if target is current tail [ECX+0x10]:\n     - Update tail to target->prev [EDX+0x10]\n     - Clear tail's next pointer [EDI]\n  6. Else (middle node):\n     - Unlink: target->prev->next = target->next\n     - Unlink: target->next->prev = target->prev\n     - Clear target's prev/next pointers\n  7. If target not null:\n     - If target->next [ESI+0x8] is null, call FUN_6f878859(0xffffffff)\n     - Zero target->tile field [EDX+0x42]\n     - Zero target->reserved [EAX+0x8]\n     - Move target to free list [ECX+0x14] and [ECX+0x18]\n  8. Decrement list count [ECX+0x8]\n\nParameters:\n  pListHeader (ECX)  - Pointer to list header structure with counts, head/tail pointers\n  nIndex (EDX)       - Index of item to remove in list\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies list in place, moves item to free list\n\nStructure Layout (assumed):\n  Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n  0x8   |4   |count|int |Number of items in active list\n  0xc   |4   |head |ptr |First node in doubly-linked list\n  0x10  |4   |tail |ptr |Last node in doubly-linked list\n  0x14  |4   |free |ptr |Head of free list\n  0x18  |4   |fTail|ptr |Tail of free list\n  0x1c  |4   |base |ptr |Base address for array storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
