      "name": "CleanupGlideTextureBuffer",
      "signature": "void CleanupGlideTextureBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases the Glide texture management buffer allocated at initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pvGlideTextureBuffer is non-NULL\n  2. If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation(NULL, 0x3E, filename)\n  3. Clear g_pvGlideTextureBuffer to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pvGlideTextureBuffer is NULL, function returns immediately without cleanup\n  - Passes 0x3E (62) to ReleasePoolAllocation for pool tracking\n  - Clears pointer after deallocation to prevent use-after-free",
