      "name": "InitializeGlideTextureCache",
      "signature": "void InitializeGlideTextureCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the Glide texture cache by computing scaling factors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize loop counter ECX = 0xfffff000 (-4096 decimal)\n  2. Iterate while ECX + 0x1000 < 0x2000:\n    a. Clamp ECX to range [0, 0xbb7] (2999 decimal)\n    b. Calculate scaling factor: 0x2ee000 / (clipped_value - 0xfffff448)\n    c. Write result to cache array via g_pGlideTextureCache pointer\n    d. Increment loop counter ECX\n  3. Set g_dwGlideTextureCacheSize = 0x100 (256)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles both negative and large ECX values via clamping\n  - Uses IDIV for division calculation (sets EDX remainder)\n  - Cache writes indexed by ESI (incremented by 4 each iteration)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
