      "name": "DrawSmackVideoQuads",
      "signature": "void DrawSmackVideoQuads(int * pSmackHandle, int nFrameHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws textured quads for Smack video frame rendering using Glide 3dfx API.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Configure Glide render state: color combine, alpha blend, texture filter\n    2. Disable chromakey for solid rendering\n    3. Extract X position from pSmackHandle[2] (offset 0x8)\n    4. Extract Y position from pSmackHandle[3] (offset 0xc)\n    5. Clamp first quad height to 0x100 (256) pixels maximum\n    6. Setup first quad vertices covering top portion (0 to 256 pixels)\n    7. Bind first texture (g_pIntroTexture1) at g_dwSpriteBufferBaseOffset\n    8. Draw first quad with grDrawVertexArrayContiguous (GR_TRIANGLE_FAN, 4 verts)\n    9. Setup second quad vertices for remaining portion (256 to nFrameHeight)\n    10. Bind second texture (g_pIntroTexture2) at g_dwSpriteBufferNextOffset\n    11. Draw second quad with grDrawVertexArrayContiguous\n    12. Re-enable chromakey mode\n\n  Parameters:\n    pSmackHandle (ECX) - Pointer to Smack control structure\n      [2]: nXPos - X screen position for video (offset 0x8)\n      [3]: nYPos - Y screen position for video (offset 0xc)\n    nFrameHeight (EDX) - Total height of video frame in pixels\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - If nFrameHeight <= 0x100 (256), first quad covers entire frame\n    - Second quad height = nFrameHeight - 0x100 (256)\n    - Uses GR_TRIANGLE_FAN (5) primitive type with 4 vertices\n    - Vertex stride is 0x1c (28) bytes matching GrVertex structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:a81a430cbb13feb722f0e81ab6bd5b55",
