      "name": "CleanupGlideBuffers",
      "signature": "void CleanupGlideBuffers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases Glide rendering system buffer allocations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if decompression buffer pointer is non-NULL\n2. If non-NULL, call ReleasePoolAllocation with size 0x74 (116)\n3. Clear decompression buffer pointer to NULL\n4. Check if highlight buffer pointer is non-NULL\n5. If non-NULL, call ReleasePoolAllocation with size 0x7a (122)\n6. Clear highlight buffer pointer to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Gracefully handles NULL pointers (no action if already NULL)\n  - Both buffers use same pool allocator (0x6f881b90)\n  - Called during Glide window closure cleanup",
