      "name": "DrawCelFrameWithMode",
      "signature": "dword DrawCelFrameWithMode(CelFileInfo * pCelInfo, int nOffsetX, dword dwParam3, int nDrawMode, dword dwParam5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Draws a CEL frame with a specified graphical mode and rendering parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data for the given index\n  2. Validate that CEL file info is available\n  3. Query CEL file properties (table index, height, mode, width)\n  4. Validate rendering bounds against screen dimensions\n  5. Calculate texture dimensions for the CEL data\n  6. Load and draw CEL texture with specified color parameters\n  7. Apply rendering mode (alpha blending, color constants, dither)\n  8. Draw final rendered frame at specified coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  pCelInfo (ECX)    - Pointer to CelFileInfo structure containing CEL data\n  nOffsetX (EDX)    - X offset coordinate for drawing on screen\n  dwParam3          - Additional parameter for texture configuration\n  nDrawMode         - Drawing mode (0-7): affects alpha blend and color settings\n  dwParam5          - Additional texture/color parameter\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Rendering failed or bounds validation failed\n  1 - Frame successfully drawn",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
