      "name": "RenderCelFrameVertices",
      "signature": "void RenderCelFrameVertices(CelFile * pCelFile, int nScreenX, int nScreenY, dword dwPaletteIndex, int nPaletteOffset, int nPaletteAdjustment)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a CEL frame as a textured quad with palette and scale adjustments.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Set graphics state: color combine enabled, texture filtering enabled\n    2. Determine vertex color from palette data (0xAABBGGRR format)\n       - If palette offset provided, use custom palette entry\n       - Otherwise use default palette index\n    3. Extract scale factors from tables (g_aScaleFactorsX, g_aScaleFactorsY)\n    4. Calculate texture coordinates by scaling frame dimensions\n    5. Query background color to determine opacity handling\n    6. If background is colored and cache scaling != 0x100:\n       - Apply texture cache scaling (0x100) to all dimensions via IMUL/SAR\n    7. Build vertex array with computed positions (nScreenX, nScreenY)\n    8. Set all vertices to opaque alpha (1.0 = 0x3f800000)\n    9. Call grDrawVertexArrayContiguous to render textured quad\n    10. Reset dither mode to mode 2\n\n  Parameters:\n    pCelFile (ECX):  Pointer to CelFile with dimension and offset fields\n    nScreenX (EDX):  Screen X coordinate for quad top-left corner\n    nScreenY:        Screen Y coordinate for quad top-left corner\n    dwPaletteIndex:  Palette index used if nPaletteOffset is zero\n    nPaletteOffset:  Byte offset into palette data (zero = use index)\n    nPaletteAdjustment: Color adjustment value (unused in this context)\n\n  Returns:\n    void (renders to current graphics surface)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:6debb80bc95675e1c46d63afae36a03f",
