      "name": "RenderCelFrame",
      "signature": "void RenderCelFrame(CelFileInfo * pCelFile, int nY, int nX, uint dwScale, int nYOffset, int nRenderMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a CEL frame sprite to the display buffer with mode-dependent visual effects.\n\nAlgorithm\n  1. Configure rendering mode via alpha blending and dithering settings based on nRenderMode\n  2. Load CEL frame data and retrieve CEL file information structure\n  3. Build CelFile stack structure with metadata (dimensions, offsets, frame indices)\n  4. Calculate texture dimensions from CEL sprite metadata\n  5. Load texture into video memory and retrieve rendering bounds\n  6. Apply clipping adjustments based on graphics background color mode\n  7. Render CEL frame vertices with final screen coordinates and transformations\n\nParameters\n  pCelFile  CEL file header pointer (ECX) - resource containing sprite frame data\n  nY        Y screen coordinate (EDX) - vertical position for rendering\n  nX        X offset (Stack +0x4) - horizontal offset adjustment\n  dwScale   Scale/clipping height (Stack +0x8) - pixels to clip from top of sprite\n  nYOffset  Y offset to preserve (Stack +0xc) - pixels to keep at bottom boundary\n  nRenderMode  Blend mode selector (Stack +0x10, 0-7) - selects visual effect\n\nReturns\n  void - no explicit return value\n\nSpecial Cases\n  - If pCelFile is null after loading, calls FUN_6f878859 for default CEL recovery\n  - Background color mode (0=transparent, else=opaque) affects clipping coordinate system\n  - When dwScale > 0, texture coordinates are adjusted for partial sprite rendering",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
