      "name": "RotateQueueNode",
      "signature": "void RotateQueueNode(void * pQueue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Rotates a doubly-linked list queue by moving nodes between active and free lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if queue is empty (nSize == nCapacity)\n  2. If not empty, move next node from free list to active list\n  3. Insert node at end of active list (doubly-linked)\n  4. Increment active count\n  5. Return if node marker is -1 (end of allocation)\n  6. If empty, move nodes from active list back to free list\n  7. Decrement active count until queue is empty again\n  8. Repeat until all nodes processed\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: pQueue - Pointer to queue structure (queue handle/context)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; modifies queue in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - FogAssert() called at line 0x9d if free list is NULL\n  - FUN_6f878859() called to allocate new node if needed\n  - Handles linked list with NULL node markers (-1 value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
