      "name": "RemoveLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "void * RemoveLinkedListNode(void * pList, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if list head (param_1 + 0xc) is null - return 0 if empty\n  2. Check if tail (param_1 + 0x1c) is null - allocate new tail if needed\n  3. Calculate target node address: tail + nIndex * 0x14\n  4. Remove node by updating prev/next pointers in linked list\n  5. Clear the removed node's forward/backward links\n  6. Return pointer to removed node\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: pList - pointer to list container structure\n  EDX: nIndex - zero-based index of node to remove\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: pointer to removed node, or 0 if list was empty\n\nStructure Layout (List Node at offset):\n  Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n  0x0c   | 4    | head  | ptr  | Pointer to first node\n  0x10   | 4    | tail  | ptr  | Pointer to last node\n  0x1c   | 4    | size  | ptr  | Pointer to allocation info\n  \nNode Structure (0x14 bytes per node):\n  Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n  0x0c   | 4    | prev  | ptr  | Previous node pointer\n  0x10   | 4    | next  | ptr  | Next node pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
