      "name": "InitializeRangeTable",
      "signature": "int InitializeRangeTable(RangeTable * pTable, int nRangeStart, int nRangeEnd, dword dwElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a range table with linked list nodes for managing ranges.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate element count = (nRangeEnd - nRangeStart) / dwElementSize\n  2. Calculate total allocation size = count * 0x1c (28 bytes per node)\n  3. Allocate memory via FogMemAlloc and zero-initialize all bytes\n  4. For each node in the table:\n     - Set node index and start offset\n     - Link forward (pNext) and backward (pPrev) pointers\n     - Update range offsets in increments of dwElementSize\n  5. If UMA is not supported, mark busy elements for ranges with addr < 0x200000\n  6. Remove trailing nodes if their address exceeds 0x200000 limit\n\nParameters:\n  pTable (ECX) - Pointer to RangeTable structure to initialize\n  nRangeStart (EDX) - Starting offset/address of the range\n  nRangeEnd (Stack+4) - Ending offset/address of the range\n  dwElementSize (Stack+8) - Size of each element/step in the range\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = nRangeStart + (element_count * dwElementSize) [end address]\n  \nSide Effects:\n  Modifies pTable structure with initialized node pointers and counts\n  Allocates memory for node table\n  May modify element counts if UMA validation fails",
