      "name": "RemoveNodeFromCache",
      "signature": "void RemoveNodeFromCache(void * pCache, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked list cache by index\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Validate cache has >1 items (offset 0x8)\n    2. Validate index != 0 (invalid hardware address)\n    3. Validate index < cache max items (offset 0x4)\n    4. Validate index >= 1\n    5. Calculate node address: base + (index * 0x1c)\n    6. If node is head (offset 0xc): update head to node.prev\n    7. Else if node is tail (offset 0x10): update tail to node.next\n    8. Else (middle node): link prev.next = node.next and next.prev = node.prev\n    9. If head becomes NULL, set head = tail = node\n    10. Clear all node link pointers (offsets 0x14 and 0x18)\n\n  Parameters:\n    pCache (ECX): Pointer to cache structure containing list metadata\n    nIndex (EDX): 1-based index of node to remove (0 is invalid/error)\n\n  Returns:\n    void (modifies cache structure in-place, no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
