      "name": "RenderTileIsometric",
      "signature": "uint RenderTileIsometric(TileProject * pTile, int nWorldX, int nWorldY, byte bUnknown, int nColorValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Renders an isometric tile projection with vertex array drawing\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize tile component reference from pTile array entry\n  2. Load tile cell coordinates and convert to isometric world space\n  3. Calculate 4 vertex positions for the tile diamond using fixed offsets (0x20000, 0x38000, etc)\n  4. Call WorldToScreen for each vertex to convert to screen coordinates\n  5. Test if any vertex is within visible screen bounds\n  6. If visible: process tile component, compute vertex colors, build vertex array\n  7. Draw vertex array using grDrawVertexArray with 4 vertices x 10 array entries\n\nParameters:\n  pTile (ECX):       Pointer to TileProject structure containing tile cell array\n  nWorldX (EDX):     World X coordinate shifted left 0xd (multiply by 0x2000)\n  nWorldY (Stack+4): World Y coordinate shifted left 0xd (multiply by 0x2000)\n  bUnknown (Stack+8): Byte value passed to SetColorFromPalette (color control)\n  nColorValue (Stack+c): Integer value for color computation\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0 if tile array is empty or no tiles rendered\n  EAX = 1 if at least one tile was rendered and vertex array drawn",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:d2f2e256ab7a1e800fa911e517dbf314",
