      "name": "CheckProcessorFeatureSupport",
      "signature": "void CheckProcessorFeatureSupport(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Checks processor feature support through dynamic loading of IsProcessorFeaturePresent API\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load KERNEL32 module handle using GetModuleHandleA\n2. Validate module handle returned successfully\n3. Get IsProcessorFeaturePresent function address via GetProcAddress  \n4. Validate function pointer obtained successfully\n5. Call IsProcessorFeaturePresent with feature ID 0 (floating point on chip)\n6. Return normally after feature check\n7. If API unavailable, call fallback function FUN_1001ddf7\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs feature detection side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0: Processor feature ID for floating point unit presence\n- Fallback path: If KERNEL32 or IsProcessorFeaturePresent unavailable, uses FUN_1001ddf7\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL module handle: Continues to fallback function\n- NULL function pointer: Continues to fallback function  \n- API not available: Graceful fallback to alternative implementation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
