      "name": "FormatFloatingPointExponent",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatingPointExponent(char * szBuffer, int nPrecision, int nUpperCase, int * pnFloatInfo, char cHasSign)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats a floating-point number in scientific notation (e.g., \"1.234e+005\").\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If cHasSign, call sign-handling helper FUN_6fdd8130\n2. Write minus sign if pnFloatInfo[0] == 0x2d ('-')\n3. If nPrecision > 0, shift mantissa and insert decimal point\n4. Append \"e+000\" exponent template via FUN_6fddb6c0 (strcpy)\n5. If nUpperCase, change 'e' to 'E' (0x45)\n6. Convert exponent value pnFloatInfo[1]-1 to digits in-place\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nPrecision (int): Decimal places (0 = no decimal point)\n- nUpperCase (int): Use 'E' instead of 'e' if non-zero\n- pnFloatInfo (int*): Float info struct [0]=sign, [1]=exponent, [3]=significand ptr\n- cHasSign (char): Include sign prefix handling\n\nReturns:\n- szBuffer pointer (for chaining)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' (minus sign)\n- 0x45 (69): ASCII 'E' (uppercase exponent)\n- 99, 9: Exponent digit thresholds for 100s and 10s place",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:16032f476aba0e42e163f0f1660d4b55",
