      "name": "FormatFloatString",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatString(char * szBuffer, size_t nPrecision, int * pnDigitInfo, char cTrailingZero)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats a number string with sign, leading zeros, and decimal point.\nUsed by CvtDoubleToFixedStr for printf %f style formatting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If cTrailingZero set and (digits-1)==precision, append trailing '0' and null\n2. If sign is negative (0x2d), write '-' prefix and advance cursor\n3. If digit count < 1, shift buffer and insert leading '0'\n4. Otherwise advance cursor past existing digits\n5. If precision > 0, shift buffer and insert decimal point\n6. If digit count negative, fill zeros after decimal point via memset\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer containing mantissa digit string\n- nPrecision (size_t): Number of decimal places to format\n- pnDigitInfo (int*): Pointer to two-element array [sign, digitCount]\n- cTrailingZero (char): Flag to append trailing zero when needed\n\nReturns:\n- szBuffer pointer unchanged\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0' zero digit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:4d68ba1e7cd9cf93c647a05c5aeb72ee",
