      "name": "DisplayRuntimeError",
      "signature": "void DisplayRuntimeError(dword dwErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles runtime errors and displays error information to user or console.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Search error handler table (g_aErrorHandlerTable) for matching error code\n  2. If found, check error handler mode (g_dwErrorHandlerMode):\n     - Mode 0x1: Write error description to console (STDOUT)\n     - Mode 0x0: Check error state flag (g_dwErrorStateFlag) to decide\n     - Mode other: Display error dialog with detailed information\n  3. For dialog mode, retrieve module file path using GetModuleFileNameA()\n  4. Truncate path if exceeds 0x3c (60) characters, append \"...\"\n  5. Construct error message: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: [path]\n[error description]\"\n  6. Display dialog via FUN_6f87d20f() with MB_ICONSTOP | MB_OK flags (0x12010)\n\nParameters:\n  dwErrorCode [0x0] - Error code to handle (index into error handler table)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return normally (terminates via exit/dialog)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error code 0xfc (252): Skipped, no action taken\n  - Module path fetch failure: Uses default message \"<program name unknown>\"\n  - Path truncation: Limits to 0x3c characters, appends \"...\"\n\nStructure Layout - Error Handler Table Entry:\n  Offset | Size | Field            | Type   | Description\n  0x0    | 0x4  | dwErrorCode      | dword  | Error code identifier\n  0x4    | 0x4  | pszDescription   | ptr    | Pointer to error message string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ff7880d11813b11bf7ac9bc241be5c60",
