      "name": "AdjustFileBufferBounds",
      "signature": "uint AdjustFileBufferBounds(int nHeapHandle, int * pAllocInfo, byte * pBlockStart, uint dwRequestedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Allocates or resizes a heap memory block\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract current block size from byte at pBlockStart\n  2. Calculate heap metadata descriptor index from pAllocInfo and nHeapHandle base\n  3. If dwRequestedSize < current size (shrinking):\n     - Update block size field to new size\n     - Calculate freed bytes (current - new)\n     - Add freed bytes to heap free count at descriptor[0]\n     - Mark descriptor[1] with 0xf1 sentinel\n  4. If dwRequestedSize == current size: return 0 (no change needed)\n  5. If dwRequestedSize > current size (expanding):\n     - Validate expansion region [pBlockStart + current..requested] contains only zeros\n     - Check that expansion doesn't exceed boundary (pAllocInfo + 0xf8)\n     - Update block size to new size\n     - Update allocation pointer if pointer falls within expanded region\n     - Calculate null-terminator position for string handling if needed\n  6. Add freed bytes to heap free count (accounts for shrinking or expansion reuse)\n  7. Return 1 on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nParameters:\n  nHeapHandle (EBP+0x8): Heap descriptor base address (int)\n  pAllocInfo (EBP+0xc): Pointer to allocation info structure\n  pBlockStart (EBP+0x10): Pointer to first byte of block (contains current size)\n  dwRequestedSize (EBP+0x14): Requested new size in bytes (uint)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1: Block allocation/resize succeeded\n  EAX=0: Operation failed (expansion area not zero-filled, bounds exceeded, or no resize needed)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
