      "name": "CopyThreeIntegers",
      "signature": "void CopyThreeIntegers(int nDestination, uint * pSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies three consecutive 32-bit integers from source to destination using offset-based addressing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset between destination address and source pointer address\n2. Initialize counter to 3 for three integer copy operations\n3. Enter copy loop:\n   a. Read current source integer value\n   b. Store value at destination using calculated offset + current source position\n   c. Advance source pointer by 4 bytes (one integer)\n   d. Decrement counter\n   e. Continue while counter > 0\n4. Return when all three integers copied\n\nParameters:\n- nDestination (int): Target memory address where integers will be copied\n- pSource (uint *): Source pointer to array of 32-bit unsigned integers\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, performs in-place memory copy operation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function always copies exactly 3 integers (12 bytes total)\n- Uses pointer arithmetic with offset calculation for addressing\n- No bounds checking or validation performed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x3 (3): Fixed number of integers to copy\n- 0x4 (4): Size increment per iteration (sizeof(uint))\n- 0x1 (1): Decrement value for loop counter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
