      "name": "ZeroFloatComponents",
      "signature": "void ZeroFloatComponents(uint * pFloatComponents)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Zeros three consecutive 32-bit floating-point component values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load target address into EDI from stack parameter\n2. Clear EAX register to zero\n3. Store zero to first component [EDI] and increment EDI by 4\n4. Store zero to second component [EDI+4] and increment EDI by 4  \n5. Store zero to third component [EDI+8] and increment EDI by 4\n6. Restore EDI register and return\n\nParameters:\npFloatComponents (uint *): Pointer to array of 3 consecutive 32-bit values representing floating-point components (mantissa, exponent, sign or similar decomposition)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses optimized STOSD instruction for efficient zeroing of 32-bit values\nAssembly utilizes string instruction auto-increment for consecutive memory writes",
