      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize character classification table for the specified code page.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Acquire global allocator (0x19)\n  2. Check if CodePage already cached - return 0 if found\n  3. If CodePage not found, determine table index and load from predefined table\n  4. If index valid, copy classification table directly\n  5. Otherwise, call GetCPInfo() for Windows code page handling\n  6. For single-byte code pages: set bits 0x8 for all values 0x01-0xFF\n  7. For multi-byte code pages: set bits 0x4 for lead byte ranges\n  8. Store cache values and return\n  \n  Parameters:\n  nCodePage (EAX): Code page identifier (e.g., 932 for Shift-JIS)\n  \n  Returns:\n  EAX: 0 for success, 0xFFFFFFFF if error condition detected\n  \n  Globals Modified:\n  g_aCharClassTable: 256-entry char classification array (0x6f887620)\n  DAT_6f8874f0: Cached code page\n  DAT_6f887724: Multi-byte handling flag\n  _DAT_6f88750c: MBCS enabled flag",
