      "name": "ConvertExtendedFloatToDecimalString",
      "signature": "int ConvertExtendedFloatToDecimalString(uint dwMantissaLow, uint dwMantissaHigh, uint dwExponentAndSign, int nPrecision, byte byFormatFlags, FloatFormatState * pFormatState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts extended precision floating-point number to formatted decimal string representation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 96-bit mantissa buffer with marker bytes (0xCC pattern + 0xFB3F signature)\n2. Extract sign bit from dwExponentAndSign and set format result sign character\n3. Check for zero value: if mantissa and exponent are zero, format as \"0\" and return success\n4. Handle IEEE 754 special values when biased exponent equals 0x7FFF:\n   - Infinity: mantissa = 0x80000000,0x00000000 -> format as \"1#INF\"\n   - Indeterminate: mantissa = 0xC0000000,0x00000000 with sign -> format as \"1#IND\"  \n   - Quiet NaN: mantissa has bit 30 set -> format as \"1#QNAN\"\n   - Signaling NaN: other non-zero mantissa -> format as \"1#SNAN\"\n5. Calculate decimal exponent using approximation: ((exp>>8 + (mantH>>24)*2) * 77 + exp*19728 - 0x134312F4) >> 16\n6. Normalize mantissa to range [1.0, 10.0) by left-shifting 8 positions initially\n7. Apply exponent adjustment: left shift for positive, right shift for negative\n8. Determine effective precision: use nPrecision directly or nPrecision + calculated exponent if format flags indicate\n9. Generate decimal digits by repeated multiply-by-10 and extract high digit:\n   - Left shift mantissa 3 times (multiply by 8), then add original (total multiply by 10)\n   - Extract high byte as decimal digit, add ASCII '0' offset\n   - Continue for nEffectivePrecision + 1 digits\n10. Perform decimal rounding based on final digit:\n    - If last digit > '4': round up by incrementing previous digits, handling carry propagation\n    - If rounding causes overflow: increment exponent and set mantissa to \"1\"\n11. Trim trailing zeros from right, ensuring at least one digit remains\n12. Store final exponent, digit count, and null-terminated digit string in format result structure\n\nParameters:\ndwMantissaLow: Low 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa\ndwMantissaHigh: High 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa  \ndwExponentAndSign: Bits 0-14 contain biased exponent, bit 15 contains sign (1=negative)\nnPrecision: Desired number of decimal places after decimal point\nbyFormatFlags: Bit 0 = adjust precision based on exponent magnitude\npFormatState: Pointer to FloatFormatState structure for formatted output\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful conversion with normal numeric result\n0 on special value detection (infinity, NaN) - string contains special format\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero input (all mantissa and exponent bits zero) formats as single \"0\" digit\n- Biased exponent 0x7FFF indicates IEEE 754 special values requiring string constants\n- Maximum precision clamped to 21 decimal digits (0x15) to prevent buffer overflow\n- Negative exponent adjustment requires right-shifting mantissa with precision loss\n- Decimal rounding may increment exponent when carry propagates through all digits\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FFF: Maximum biased exponent indicating IEEE 754 special values\n0x8000: Sign bit mask in dwExponentAndSign parameter  \n0x80000000: Canonical infinity mantissa high word\n0xC0000000: Indeterminate NaN mantissa pattern with sign bit\n0x40000000: Quiet NaN detection bit in mantissa high word\n0x3FFE: Bias adjustment for exponent normalization threshold\n0x134312F4: Negative constant in decimal exponent approximation formula\n0x4D10, 0x4D: Multiplication constants for exponent calculation (19728, 77 decimal)\n0xCC: Debug marker byte pattern for mantissa buffer initialization  \n0xFB3F: Extended precision mantissa signature bytes\n0x15: Maximum allowed precision (21 decimal digits)\n\nStructure Layout:\nFloatFormatState layout (16 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x00  |  2   | nExponent  | short| Decimal exponent for scientific notation\n+0x02  |  1   | cSign      | char | Sign character: 0x20 (' ') or 0x2D ('-')  \n+0x03  |  1   | byDigitCount| byte | Number of significant decimal digits generated\n+0x04  | 12   | szDigits   | char[]| Null-terminated decimal digit string\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid special value patterns default to \"1#QNAN\" format\n- Precision overflow beyond 21 digits silently clamped to prevent buffer corruption\n- Mantissa buffer overflow during digit generation handled by fixed iteration limit\n- Function assumes valid FloatFormatState pointer - no null pointer validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
