      "name": "MultiplyExtendedFloat96",
      "signature": "void MultiplyExtendedFloat96(int * pResult, int * pMultiplicand)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Multiply two 96-bit extended floating-point numbers with IEEE 754-style semantics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponents from both operands by masking bits 0-14 of the exponent field\n2. Calculate sign bit by XORing the sign bits (bit 15) of both operands\n3. Check for special cases: infinity (exponent >= 0x7FFF) or underflow results\n4. Validate that neither operand is zero by checking all mantissa fields\n5. Add exponents together and adjust for bias (0xC002 = 49154, bias adjustment)\n6. Perform 96-bit mantissa multiplication using 5x5 grid of 16-bit \u00d7 16-bit operations\n7. Call AddUintWithOverflowCheck for each partial product and accumulate carries\n8. Normalize the result by shifting mantissa left or right based on final exponent\n9. Handle rounding by tracking least significant bits during right shifts\n10. Check for overflow conditions and handle infinity/NaN cases\n11. Pack final result into output structure with sign, exponent, and mantissa fields\n\nParameters:\npResult (int *): Pointer to 12-byte ExtendedFloat structure for result storage\n    Structure layout: [0-3] dwMantissaLow, [4-7] dwMantissaMid, [8-11] dwMantissaHigh, [10-11] wExponentAndSign\npMultiplicand (int *): Pointer to first 96-bit extended float operand (same layout as result)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored directly in pResult structure\nSpecial return values: Zero for underflow, Infinity for overflow, preserves NaN inputs\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero operands: Returns zero with sign preservation\n- Infinity operands: Returns infinity with correct sign\n- Underflow (exponent < 0x3FC0): Returns zero\n- Overflow (exponent > 0x7FFE): Returns infinity (0x7FFF8000)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FFF - Maximum exponent value (infinity marker)\n0x8000 - Sign bit mask for exponent field  \n0x7FFFFFFF - Mantissa high bit mask (removes sign extension)\n0xBFFE - Maximum valid intermediate exponent (49150)\n0x3FC0 - Minimum valid result exponent after bias (16320)\n0xC002 - Exponent bias adjustment (49154)\n0x1FFFF - Mantissa overflow detection mask (131071)\n0x18000 - Specific overflow threshold (98304)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type    Description\n0       4     dwMantissaLow      uint    Least significant 32 bits of mantissa\n4       4     dwMantissaMid      uint    Middle 32 bits of mantissa  \n8       4     dwMantissaHigh     uint    Most significant 32 bits of mantissa\n10      2     wExponentAndSign   ushort  Bits 0-14: exponent, Bit 15: sign",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:998738fc08bb4aa7ede00cbbf5cbf652",
