      "name": "Div128By128",
      "signature": "ulonglong Div128By128(dword uDividendHi, dword uDividendLo, dword uDivisorHi, dword uDivisorLo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Performs 128-bit unsigned integer division.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If divisor high 32 bits = 0: perform simple 64-bit / 32-bit division\n  2. Otherwise: normalize both operands by right-shifting until divisor high bits = 0\n  3. Compute quotient using CONCAT(remainder_hi, quotient_lo) / divisor\n  4. Correct quotient if high-order bits were shifted (via multiplication verification)\n  5. Return 64-bit quotient in EDX:EAX\n\nParameters:\n  uDividendHi  Bits [127:96] of 128-bit dividend\n  uDividendLo  Bits [95:64] of 128-bit dividend (lower 64 bits split across EAX:EDX entry)\n  uDivisorHi   Bits [127:96] of 128-bit divisor\n  uDivisorLo   Bits [95:64] of 128-bit divisor\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX  64-bit unsigned integer quotient (bits [63:0] of result)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Division by zero: uDivisor=0 causes undefined behavior (no check)\n  - Quotient overflow: If dividend >= divisor<<64, result wraps (no exception)\n  - Divisor > dividend: Returns 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2043487ec0ce2238c03195f2d42cad4f",
