      "name": "Int64Divide",
      "signature": "dword Int64Divide(dword dwDividendLo, dword dwDividendHi, dword dwDivisorLo, dword dwDivisorHi)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Unsigned 64-bit integer division.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if divisor is zero (dividend_hi | dividend_lo)\n  2. If divisor is zero, perform standard division\n  3. If divisor is non-zero, use long division algorithm with bit shifting\n  4. Adjust result sign if needed (check high bits)\n  5. Return quotient\n\nParameters:\n  EAX (stack +8): dividend low 32 bits\n  EDX (stack +12): dividend high 32 bits (sign extension)\n  ECX (stack +16): divisor low 32 bits\n  [ESP+20]: divisor high 32 bits\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX = quotient (64-bit result)\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - Division by zero: undefined behavior\n  - Signed division requires sign adjustment",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
