      "name": "Mul64x64",
      "signature": "longlong Mul64x64(uint dwLow1, int nHigh1, uint dwLow2, int nHigh2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Multiplies two 64-bit integers using 32-bit operand pairs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if both high parts (nHigh1, nHigh2) are zero\n  2. If yes: return simple 32-bit multiply dwLow1 \u00d7 dwLow2 (fast path)\n  3. If no: compute full 64-bit product using cross-products:\n     - result_high = (dwLow1 \u00d7 dwLow2)[bits 63:32] + nHigh1 \u00d7 dwLow2 + dwLow1 \u00d7 nHigh2\n     - result_low = (dwLow1 \u00d7 dwLow2)[bits 31:0]\n  4. Return 64-bit result in EDX:EAX\n\nParameters:\n  dwLow1 [ESP+0x8]: Lower 32 bits of first multiplicand\n  nHigh1 [ESP+0xC]: Upper 32 bits of first multiplicand\n  dwLow2 [ESP+0x10]: Lower 32 bits of second multiplicand\n  nHigh2 [ESP+0x14]: Upper 32 bits of second multiplicand\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX: 64-bit product (EAX = low 32-bits, EDX = high 32-bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
