      "name": "DivideByFloatSafe",
      "signature": "void DivideByFloatSafe(float flDivisor)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Divides ST(0) by a float, handling special IEEE-754 cases safely.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if flDivisor exponent is 0x7F8 (infinity/NaN)\n2. If special value, perform FDIVR directly and return\n3. Check FPU status word bits 0x3800 (stack non-empty)\n4. If FPU stack has values, save ST(1) to temp, divide, restore\n5. Otherwise, just perform division via PassFpuValuesToDivide\n\nParameters:\n- flDivisor (float): Divisor value to divide FPU ST(0) by\n- IMPLICIT: ST(0) contains dividend on FPU stack\n\nReturns:\n- void, result left in ST(0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7F800000: IEEE-754 exponent mask for infinity/NaN detection\n- 0x3800: FPU status word stack bits (TOP field)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:269b7d5856cdb9005a57b4cc52158551",
