      "name": "ReverseDivideDouble",
      "signature": "void ReverseDivideDouble(uint dwDoubleLow, uint dwDoubleHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs FPU reverse division of ST0 by a double argument.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if double exponent is 0x7FF (infinity/NaN)\n2. If special value, perform direct FDIVR and return\n3. Check FPU status word for pending exceptions (bits 11-13)\n4. If exceptions pending, load double to ST0 and call PassFpuValuesToDivide\n5. Otherwise, save ST1, load double, call PassFpuValuesToDivide, restore ST1\n\nParameters:\n- dwDoubleLow (uint): Low 32 bits of double divisor\n- dwDoubleHigh (uint): High 32 bits of double divisor (contains exponent)\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains dividend value\n\nReturns:\n- void (result left in FPU stack)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7FF00000: IEEE 754 double infinity/NaN exponent mask\n- 0x3800: FPU status word exception flags (bits 11-13)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:269b7d5856cdb9005a57b4cc52158551",
